===Mastery Strategies===
{{MastComp|{{MastStrat|first|Active|-60|To actually use this Ability, either do it with another Cosmo (recommended) or a {{CI|Poppy|name=true}}/{{CI|Looey|name=true}}, as they all need Hearts to complete their Mastery. You can also bring a {{CI|Yatta|name=true}} to finish your fourth and sixth tasks by harvesting her candy.}}|{{MastStrat|second|Reach/do floors}}|{{MastStrat|third|Meters|3Star}}|{{MastStrat|fourth and sixth|Collect and use|Use}}|{{MastStrat|fifth|Play with Toons}}}}

==Requirement Strategies==
*For the first requirement, focus on picking up [[Research Capsules]] and extracting [[Machines]]. The Machine and Capsule count increases the further you descend, so you can earn more {{II|Ichor|name=true}}.
*For the second requirement, try to farm a good amount of Ichor, and buy Toons that cost less Ichor, you can have {{CI|Boxten|name=true}} or {{CI|Poppy|name=true}} for free so you can buy 3 more Toons like:{{CI|Shrimpo|name=true}}, {{CI|Finn|name=true}}, {{CI|Tisha|name=true}} and {{CI|Toodles|name=true}}.

==Strategies==
Cosmo is a supporter whose Active [[Ability]], {{AI|Cosmo|name=true}}, gives one of his {{Heart}} to another damaged [[Toon]]. As one of only four Toons capable of healing at the moment, his Ability is nice in situations where a teammate is low on Hearts or at risk. Be cautious though, giving out too many Hearts will quickly put you in danger and might even cause harm to teammates in an attempt to save you.

With a good set of [[Stats]], the main issue for Cosmo is his 1{{Star}} [[Skill Check]]. The small window makes them much more difficult, and the value given makes them not very rewarding when landing them. Even though Cosmo is the fastest at extraction compared to {{CI|Bassie|name=true}}, {{CI|Blot|name=true}}, and {{CI|Shrimpo|name=true}}, all four of them still have 1 Star Skill Check, making it arduous to even get a good result on the [[Machine]]. This disadvantage can be managed by using Skill Check [[Trinkets]] like {{TI|Mime Makeup|name=true}}, {{TI|Thinking Cap|name=true}}, or {{TI|Blue Bandana|name=true}} (though note Blue Bandana slows progress down by a bit and is only recommended to newer players). On the other hand, Cosmo's above-average [[Stealth]] and mobility makes it much easier to go and heal Distractors, as outside of turning corners, distracted [[Twisteds]] will not switch targets, and even so, he can easily escape them. If you fail Skill Checks often, extracting from Treadmill Machines can be quite good, especially thanks to his higher Stamina. Due to Cosmo not filling any other niche (other than support), it is recommended for you to just wander around the map for {{Tape|name=true}} (assuming no Tape-reliant Toons are present and need them) and healing [[Items]] for later use. If the map has been scavenged already, check for teammates low on Health or find Machines to do.

He's well-suited to runs with a lot of {{Type|Main}} Toons present due to his Ability to stretch {{II|Health Kit|name=true}} twice as far for them. His long range normally can make it a bit difficult to heal the right teammate, though if in the aforementioned team setup, any heal will go towards a Toon on 1 Heart.

Cosmo's best benefit over the other healers is his Ability's secondary effect: highlighting selected teammates through walls and showing which animation they're in. Since his range is extremely long, you can keep tabs on others from a great distance. This is helpful to detect other players, such as distractors or players in need of assistance.

When looking for Items, focus on Health Kits and {{II|Bandage|name=false}}s so you can make use of your Ability more often. Since Cosmo can redistribute Hearts on the fly, consider asking your teammates to alert you if they see any so you can bring the Hearts to distractors or save them for later Floors. Also allow those in need of healing to take Items since Cosmo's higher Stamina and Stealth leave him in less danger. Since Health Kits and Bandages are quite rare, you can also look for more common but helpful Items such as {{II|Stopwatch|name=false}}es to make his Skill Check more bearable. The extra Tapes received from them can also be used to buy healing Items when they are being sold. If a non-{{Type|Main}} teammate is on 1 Heart, it is recommended to let them take a Health Kit if they happen to find it on the floor, as it instantly heals them as compared to your heal of 1 Heart.

If Bassie is in your group, try to prioritize Health Kits and give them any Bandages. The more people capable of delivering healing, the faster ailing Toons receive aid. You can also rely on Bassie to hold onto most healing Items and to heal you once your Health is low, as she out-speeds you. Leaving your heals with a Bassie can also be very beneficial in the event that {{CI|Twisted Gigi|name=true}} spawns on the floor as Bassie can repeatedly deposit and pick up the Items, rendering Twisted Gigi unable to take them with good timing.

Cosmo is great when paired with {{CI|Ginger|name=true}}, as Ginger can heal him while at low Health, essentially making him an infinite healing machine. This, however, would require a lot of Tape income for Ginger, depending on how much your team loses Hearts, so it isn't as optimal as it seems. He can also pair up with {{CI|Sprout|name=true}} but less effectively, as he can only heal with 1 Heart with his Ability for the same cost.

Overall, Cosmo's Stats make him most preferably played as a healer who utilizes his longest range out of the three to heal from a safe place, but still also decently contribute with roughly any Machine types (primarily if you don't struggle with his 1 Star Skill Check). He acts somewhat like an all-rounder in comparison to the other healers.

===Trinket Combinations===
{{Preference}}
Some [[Trinkets]] sets for Cosmo includes:

====Survivability====
*'''{{TI|Pink Bow|name=true}}/Options'''
**This Trinket enables Cosmo to outrun all Twisteds before [[Panic Mode]] besides {{CI|Twisted Dyle|name=true}} as well as reaching teammates at max speed faster {{Small|(26.9 run speed)}}. Here are some options to pair Pink Bow with;
***'''{{TI|Speedy Shoes|name=true}}''', to further improve Run Speed {{Small|(28.2 run speed)}};
***'''{{TI|Vanity Mirror|name=true}}''', to outrun every Twisted except Twisted Dyle during Panic Mode {{Small|(35 run speed)}};
***'''{{TI|Diary|name=true}}''', although quite situational, can help if there is a distractor with 4{{Star}} [[Stealth]] such as {{CI|Bassie|name=true}} so you can safely go near them to collect heals while they distract;
***'''{{TI|Savory Charm|name=true}}''', to be a tad bit safer if on 1{{Heart}}, due to Cosmo's frequent Heart loss, despite the usage of this Trinket only working once;
***'''{{TI|Train Whistle|name=true}}''', to help Cosmo avoid losing Hearts during an [[Ichor Leak]], or while {{CI|Twisted Vee|name=true}} on the Floor;
***Any of the Trinkets in the '''Extraction Section'''; etc.

====Extraction====
*The following Trinkets help Cosmo extract by dealing with his main deficiency, which is his 1{{Star}} [[Skill Check]] {{Small|(50 skill check size)}} and 3 Star [[Extraction Speed]] {{Small|(1.00 extraction speed)}}:
**'''{{TI|Vee's Remote|name=true}}''', to instantly complete [[Machines]] in dangerous locations, such as dead ends and open areas;
**'''{{TI|Mime Makeup|name=true}}''', to more safely extract by removing the danger of missing Skill Checks;
**'''{{TI|Thinking Cap|name=true}}''', to increase Skill Check Size, helping to fail less Skill Checks, though Mime Makeup can be more beneficial in some cases;
*If the player has no issues with small Skill Checks, they may consider using '''{{TI|Magnifying Glass|name=true}}''' or '''{{TI|Participation Award|name=true}}''' to help with [[Machine]] extraction more easily, even if the Skill Check window is far smaller. Though, do note that if the player has lag/missing frames, they may want to consider other Trinkets for team progression.
**Any Trinkets listed in the '''Survivability/Mobility''' section, to help with survival.

====Ability/Support====
*'''{{TI|Ghost Snakes In A Can|name=true}}''', to reduce {{AI|Cosmo|name=true}}'s [[Ability]] cooldown {{Small|(55s)}};
**'''{{TI|Sweet Charm|name=true}}''', to further reduce '''Sharing is Caring'''<nowiki/>'s cooldown, though only by a small amount as the Trinket works with percentages {{Small|(50.2s)}}.
*'''{{TI|Memory Locket|name=true}}''', to help highlight any healing [[Items]] on the Floor, making it easier to heal other teammates;
**This Trinket is best used in unorganized runs where heals may be easily taken by other players.
*'''{{TI|Dandy Plush|name=true}}''', to help you buy healing Items if a [[Toon]] that needs {{Tape|name=true}} (e.g. {{CI|Ginger|name=true}}) is present, letting you still have sufficient Tapes from usual activities for healing Items.

'''Note: It isn't recommended to use Tape-giving Trinkets such as {{TI|Fancy Purse|name=true}}, as it is a one-time use Trinket, and wastes a Trinket slot if {{CI|Dandy|name=true}} does not sell a {{II|Health Kit|name=false}} or {{II|Bandage|name=false}} on an earlier floor before you have 100 Tapes. Trinkets such as Dandy Plush are more beneficial in the long run, as their effects last the whole run.'''

