==Trivia==
*Cosmo's name and design is derived from the dessert food {{wp|Cosmic Brownies}}, as he has colorful, star-shaped sprinkles sporting his cheeks similar to Cosmic Brownies. Also, the word "cosmo" is the noun form of the adjective, "cosmic". The term "cosmo" is also derived from the name for a celestial object—whether a planet, star or galaxy—a "cosmos".
**According to his dialogue with {{CI|Glisten|name=true}}, the sprinkles on his cheeks are not makeup.
**The sprinkles on his body are also possibly a reference to the stars scattered across the cosmos, making his connection to them even stronger.
**Alternatively, it could be derived from the word 'cosmopolitan', which means "including or containing things from many different areas", which could reflect how you need ≥4 [[Toons]] to buy him or his generosity.
**On top of that, Cosmo is admittedly a mix of a {{wp|Swiss Roll}} and a Cosmic Brownie.
*Cosmo is {{CI|Sprout|name=true}}'s best friend, which has been established and shown in dialogues, [[Posters]], and other miscellaneous things that allude to it, like how:
**Cosmo and Sprout have matching bracelets for Trinkets ({{TI|Sweet Charm|name=true}} and {{TI|Savory Charm|name=true}}).
**Cosmo and Sprout have multiple matching [[Skins]], such as {{Skin|Caramel Drizzle Cosmo}} & {{Skin|Salted Caramel Sprout}}) and {{Skin|Berry Roll Cosmo}} & {{Skin|ChocoBerry Sprout}}.
**Cosmo and Sprout's corresponding [[Twisteds]] have similar [[Ichor]] patterns; Cosmo only has Ichor on his right arm and eye, while Sprout has Ichor everywhere except his right arm and eye.
**Cosmo's Twisted's [[Research]] description mentions Cosmo twisting due to seperation from his best friend, referring to Sprout.
**Their [[Abilities]] are able to heal a [[Toon]] by 1{{Heart}}.
**They were optimized on the same [[Update]].
***Sprout and Cosmo are the first [[Toons]] that were not released in [[Changelog|v0.1]] to receive an optimized model.
****Additionally, Cosmo, alongside [[Poppy]] and [[Boxten]] are the first Common Toons to get optimized.
**They share similar hobbies: baking/cooking.
**Both of them are based of foods and are the second Toons to be so, with the first being {{CI|Shrimpo|name=true}}, the third being {{CI|Ginger|name=true}}, the fourth being {{CI|Eggson|name=true}} and {{CI|Cocoa|name=true}}, and the fifth being {{CI|Gourdy|name=true}}.
**When [[Twisted Sprout]] follows [[Twisted Cosmo]] around, he stops to let Twisted Sprout catch up.
*Cosmo and [[Ginger]] are cousins.
**Their relativity follows the pattern of {{Type|Uncommon}} [[Event Toons]] being related to a base game [[Toon]].
*Cosmo likes to stargaze sometimes, as stated in a QnA stream by [[Qwel]].
*Cosmo might not be too good with the oven. This can be implied through his interaction with {{CI|Toodles|name=true}} as well as his and [[Sprout]]'s TV animation and CCTV footage, when the oven set on fire, which also could've led to his dream about fire mentioned in his interaction with [[Astro]].
*Prior to his optimization, Cosmo's cookies that appeared when he healed someone used to match his color and had sprinkles that matched the color of his star-shaped sprinkles on his cheeks for each of his [[Skins]] he had at the time.
*As said by [[Qwel]] during the 2025 New Years stream, Cosmo can't sleep sideways due to the shape of his head.
*It is possible that the reason at least one of Cosmo's hands are almost always holding onto his head is because it's too big for his body, thus possibly causing some issues. This has yet to be confirmed or denied in any way possible, however, as in a lot of artworks and TV animations he's seen just fine with his hands in a different position.
**This could be a result of cartoon logic not being exactly applicable to the real world, hence why he only seems to do this in his 3d model.
**Another possible explanation of this could be the animators not caring about this and wanting Cosmo to use both hands, especially as the constant drawing of holding his head is unneeded.
*Cosmo seems to be shaken up about having gumballs for eyes on cookies, as mentioned in an interaction between [[Sprout]] and {{CI|Flutter|name=true}}, and Cosmo's interaction with {{CI|Poppy|name=true}} where he refuses to make cookies of her with gumballs for eyes.
**This may likely be a reference to [https://spongebob.fandom.com/wiki/SpongeBob_SquarePants_Popsicle?file=Popsicle-fails-spongebob-22.jpg Spongebob popsicles], specifically the ones with gumball eyes. The popsicles with gumball eyes are known to come out majorly deformed and melt. This is what happened with the [[Flutter]] cookies, its eyes melting, extra designs cracking, and the overall appearance causing Cosmo to cry "for a whole week" (stated in [[Sprout]]'s interaction with [[Flutter]]).
*Cosmo and [[Ginger]]'s [[Abilities]] used to be nearly identical, with the only differences being Cosmo having a shorter cooldown and range than Ginger.
**However since the [[2025 Christmas Event]], Ginger has gotten a rework to heal full [[Hearts]] by holding the Ability for 5 seconds, needing 100 {{Tape|name=true}}, and having a very short range.
***Because of this, Cosmo has gotten Ginger's large range before rework.
*Cosmo is one of seven [[Toons]] to have one of their dialogues shown behind the scenes, with the other six being {{CI|Boxten|name=true}}, [[Connie]], [[Flutter]], [[Glisten]], [[Shrimpo]], and {{CI|Vee|name=true}}.
*Cosmo is the first [[Toon]] to extract with one hand.
*Cosmo's head is somewhat polygonal. While this isn't very noticeable, if you look sideways, you'll notice his eyes somewhat clip on the edges.
*Cosmo's [[Sweet Charm]] from his idle animation is stored in his body, only taken out when the idle is used.
**[[Sprout]] and his [[Savory Charm]] do the same.
*Although Cosmo is one of the main cooks of [[Gardenview]], he specializes on sweets and desserts more, mainly baking cookies for the [[Toons]], as seen in some interactions and his [[Ability]], though other stuff like cakes have been made by him. Him being a cake roll/brownie and his "soft" personality compliments this too.
*Cosmo's Active [[Ability]] has a small detail where his hands touch his chest before he heals someone. This makes it look like he gives '''his Heart''' to another [[Toon]].
*Cosmo was the first created Side Character [[Toon]], which is confirmed in [[Bobette]]'s [[gossip]] about him and the "[[:File:Sprout Opens up to Astro|Sprout opening up to Astro]]" CCTV footage, making his designation '''SC-001'''.
**This makes him the second non-Main Character [[Toon]] to have a confirmed designation without a [[Roleplay]] room, the first being {{CI|Yatta|name=true}}, whose designation was revealed in a real-life event.
***The reason for his early creation was due to [[Sprout]] pestering [[Arthur]] or [[Delilah]] to create Cosmo first before starting to create the Side Characters, as Sprout felt disconnected with his Show memories.
*Cosmo is the first non-[[Event Toon]] with a seasonal [[Gamepass]] [[Skin]], being part of the [[Snow-Time Cosmetic Pack]].
**This is likely because of his relations to [[Ginger]], a Christmas Toon.
**He is also technically the first [[Toon]] to be in a Skin pack with minimal similarities with the other [[Toons]]; [[Star-Time]] has all the [[Main Character]] Toons, [[Show-Time]] has all the Toons correlating with shows, and [[Snow-Time]] should have all the Christmas Toons.
*Cosmo is the only male [[Toon]] to have 4 Star [[Stealth]].
*He is the third non-[[Main Character|Main]] Toon to have an official deluxe plush version of himself, with the first being [[Cocoa]], the second being [[Goob]], and the forth one being [[Gigi]].
**Cosmo's plush is currently the only [[Toon]] with a different facial expression from his default, with the plush having a smile, much like a large portion of his skins, while his in-game design has a frown.
*Cosmo's {{Skin|Berry Roll}} [[Skin]] has a bug where his left hand is tilted wrongly during his running animation.

